From 0ff8637b44260c326d0cbe4350b2ab4ed831cd74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 18:56:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf phase 11 patch 0137 -- wave-42 GM_VARIANT env var
 for org2mid v1/v2 A/B

Wave-42 ride-along to #18 notesoff fix: add engine-side support for
in-iter listening A/B between org2mid v1 (current) and v2 (retuned)
GM-patch tables. Per user direction 2026-05-14: ship BOTH tables in
the same iter so operator can compare across the TAS-deterministic
real-HW session instead of cycling two separate iters.

New env var: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_GM_VARIANT
  Values: "v1" | "v2" (strict-match; anything else falls back to legacy)
  Default: unset -> legacy dir (= wave-41 behavior preserved bit-for-bit)

Engine resolution table:
  SOURCE    VARIANT  ->  dir
  wiimidi   unset    ->  data/midi/      (legacy wave-41 default)
  wiimidi   v1       ->  data/midi-v1/   (org2mid v1 .mid output)
  wiimidi   v2       ->  data/midi-v2/   (org2mid v2 .mid output; retuned)
  orgmid    unset    ->  data/orgmid/    (legacy wave-41 default)
  orgmid    v1       ->  data/orgmid1/   (org2mid v1 ORGMID transcription)
  orgmid    v2       ->  data/orgmid2/   (org2mid v2 ORGMID retune)

DOS 8.3 constraint per existing patch 0109: 8 chars max in directory
basename or fopen returns EINVAL on real HW with lfn=false (silently
falls back to LOG_WARN; PLAY cell produces no music). Dir naming
chosen for 7-char max basenames:
  - "midi-v1" / "midi-v2" : 7 chars each
  - "orgmid1" / "orgmid2" : 7 chars each (NO hyphen; "orgmid-v1" at
    9 chars would replicate the patch-0109 EINVAL trap)
Asymmetric per-source naming (hyphen for midi-*, no hyphen for
orgmid*) was the deliberate trade-off team-lead approved 2026-05-14:
per-source internal consistency > cross-source symmetry; avoids
renaming the existing `data/orgmid/` dir that operator's wave-41 CF
state already depends on.

Default-OFF preservation per
[[single_lever_per_binary_or_else_attribution_impossible]]: legacy
behavior unchanged. PLAY1 (codegen parity probe) with no env vars
resolves to existing data/midi/ or data/orgmid/ exactly as wave-41
did. The GM_VARIANT env var is the only ADD; no replacement of
existing behavior. wave-41-anchor comparison preserved.

Diagnostic LOG_INFO updates: every dir-resolution path now logs
the resolved variant (`variant=v1` / `variant=v2` / `variant=(unset; legacy)`)
so post-iter log parsing can verify the right dir was hit per PLAY.
LOG_WARN fires when env var is set to a non-recognized value (typo
guard; operator gets explicit feedback instead of silent legacy
fallback).

Files:
  src/sound/SoundManager.cpp  -- dir resolution logic extended (~40 lines)
                                  + LOG_INFO message updates per branch

No CMakeLists.txt changes (env-var consumer is purely runtime).

org2mid host-side support (the v1/v2 GM-table data generation; CLI
flag --gm-table=v1|v2) lands as #19 PART A in a separate commit; this
patch is PART B only (engine env var wiring). The two patches can
land independently; engine reads from whatever .mid files exist in
the resolved dir (missing files degrade gracefully per existing
LOG_WARN at SoundManager.cpp:1082 unchanged).

docs/BOOT.md entry: separate update in parent repo (not vendor
commit) per env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md.
---
 src/sound/SoundManager.cpp | 92 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 81 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
index bf476fe..ab7f4d2 100644
--- a/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/SoundManager.cpp
@@ -373,13 +373,68 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
   // see which set was in use without diffing audio output.
   {
     const char *src = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE");
+
+    // Patch 0137 (wave 42 ride-along to #18; revised 2026-05-14 v2 per
+    // team-lead arbitration after STOP-2 surfaced wiimidi/orgmid
+    // content-collapse): GM_VARIANT env var for in-iter A/B listening
+    // between org2mid v1 and v2 GM-patch mapping tables.
+    //
+    // Design rationale (corrected from v1): GM_VARIANT controls which
+    // GM-patch table our `tools/org2mid/` host converter applies. It
+    // ONLY affects the orgmid source path -- the wiimidi source is
+    // external WiiWare GitHub content with pre-baked GM events that
+    // our converter cannot influence. v1 of this patch incorrectly
+    // produced 4 dirs treating wiimidi-vN and orgmidN as parallel
+    // axes; in practice they were byte-identical because the same
+    // converter generated both. Revised semantics: wiimidi axis
+    // ignores variant; orgmid axis honors it. 3-tool-4-output story:
+    //
+    //   SOURCE     VARIANT  ->  dir            ; provenance
+    //   wiimidi    (any)    ->  data/midi/     ; external WiiMidi GitHub
+    //   orgmid     (unset)  ->  data/orgmid/   ; Hart's ORGMID (legacy)
+    //   orgmid     v1       ->  data/orgmid1/  ; our org2mid v1 GM
+    //   orgmid     v2       ->  data/orgmid2/  ; our org2mid v2 GM
+    //
+    // DOS 8.3 dir-name constraint (per existing patch 0109): 7-char
+    // basenames work (`orgmid1`, `orgmid2`); 9-char `orgmid-v1` would
+    // EINVAL on lfn=false real HW.
+    //
+    // Default behavior preserved bit-for-bit from wave-41:
+    // - SOURCE=wiimidi + VARIANT unset -> data/midi/   (same as wave-41)
+    // - SOURCE=orgmid + VARIANT unset  -> data/orgmid/ (same as wave-41)
+    //
+    // Strict-match: only literal "v1" or "v2" engage variant; any
+    // other value (empty, "V1", "1", garbage) leaves variant unset =
+    // legacy dir.
+    //
+    // Cross-validity check: if SOURCE=wiimidi + VARIANT set, the
+    // variant is silently ignored (resolves to data/midi/) but a
+    // LOG_WARN narrates the no-op so operator sees what happened
+    // instead of being confused by perceived no-effect.
+    const char *variant = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_GM_VARIANT");
+    const bool is_v1 = variant && std::strcmp(variant, "v1") == 0;
+    const bool is_v2 = variant && std::strcmp(variant, "v2") == 0;
+    const bool variant_set = is_v1 || is_v2;
+    const char *variant_str = is_v1 ? "v1" : (is_v2 ? "v2" : "(unset; legacy)");
+
     if (src == nullptr || src[0] == '\0' || std::strcmp(src, "wiimidi") == 0)
     {
       _midi_source_dir = "midi";
-      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'wiimidi' "
-               "(default; resolves to data/midi/<name>.mid; the WiiWare "
+      if (variant_set)
+      {
+        LOG_WARN("MidiScheduler: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_GM_VARIANT={} "
+                 "is set but SOURCE=wiimidi ignores it (the WiiMidi GitHub "
+                 "set has pre-baked GM events not under our converter "
+                 "control). To engage v1/v2 GM-table A/B, also set "
+                 "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_SOURCE=orgmid. Resolving "
+                 "to data/midi/ (legacy WiiMidi).", variant_str);
+      }
+      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'wiimidi' variant={} "
+               "(resolves to data/midi/<name>.mid; the WiiWare "
                "arrangement set fetched by scripts/fetch-cs-midi.py per "
-               "docs/ASSETS.md Step 4.5).");
+               "docs/ASSETS.md Step 4.5; pre-baked GM events; variant "
+               "is a no-op on this source).",
+               variant_str);
     }
     else if (std::strcmp(src, "orgmid") == 0)
     {
@@ -393,20 +448,35 @@ bool SoundManager::init()
       // output dir. Caught by my additional smoke after team-lead
       // confirmed the dir was in tree (errno 22 not ENOENT was the
       // diagnostic clue per dos_filename_8_3.md memory).
-      _midi_source_dir = "orgmid";
-      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'orgmid' "
-               "(resolves to data/orgmid/<name>.mid; literal ORGMID "
-               "transcription set generated by scripts/build-cs-midi-"
-               "orgmid.py -- alternative to the WiiWare arrangements for "
-               "W22-WB-E A/B comparison; transposed +12 to match Cave "
-               "Story canonical pitch).");
+      //
+      // Patch 0137 (wave 42): variant suffix appended without hyphen
+      // for orgmid case to stay <=7 chars (orgmid1 / orgmid2 = 7 chars
+      // each). orgmid-v1 / orgmid-v2 would be 9 chars = same 8.3
+      // EINVAL trap as the original midi-orgmid.
+      if (is_v1)        _midi_source_dir = "orgmid1";
+      else if (is_v2)   _midi_source_dir = "orgmid2";
+      else              _midi_source_dir = "orgmid";
+      LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: MIDI source = 'orgmid' variant={} "
+               "(resolves to data/{}/<name>.mid; v1/v2 = wave-42 "
+               "org2mid GM-table A/B per operator wave-41 'thumps "
+               "and cowbell' aesthetic feedback; unset = Hart's "
+               "legacy ORGMID transcription preserved from wave-41).",
+               variant_str, _midi_source_dir);
     }
     else
     {
       _midi_source_dir = "midi";
       LOG_INFO("MidiScheduler: unrecognized SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_"
                "SOURCE value '{}'; falling back to 'wiimidi' (data/midi/). "
-               "Recognized values: wiimidi (default) | orgmid.", src);
+               "Recognized values: wiimidi (default) | orgmid. Variant={} "
+               "ignored in fallback path.", src, variant_str);
+    }
+
+    if (variant && variant[0] != '\0' && !variant_set)
+    {
+      LOG_WARN("MidiScheduler: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDI_GM_VARIANT "
+               "value '{}' is not recognized; recognized values: v1 | v2. "
+               "Falling back to legacy dir (variant unset).", variant);
     }
   }
 
